cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these orbits or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "dreikoerper: a search engine for periodic orbits of the planar three-body problem, and its finds"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Habl
    given-names: Felix
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ne0nk3k/dreikoerper"
version: "1.0.0"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
keywords:
  - three-body problem
  - periodic orbits
  - linear stability
  - celestial mechanics
  - high-precision numerics
abstract: >-
  Periodic orbits of the planar three-body problem with zero angular
  momentum that are in none of the published lists, each verified to
  30 digits, with linear stability from the monodromy matrix. Among them
  a linearly stable orbit at masses 1 : 1 : 4 (T = 53.2548543044, stability
  indices 0.0501 and -0.0599). Includes the search engine, the
  30-digit verification and test batteries against published
  high-precision data. Code and computations were written with Claude,
  an AI model by Anthropic.
